#: processes/feature-staging.bpmn:19
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Runs all three entry points — stage, cleanup, cleanup-dispatch — as one actor because none of the work in any of them needs judgement; the one step that does, confirming a dispatch deletion, was carved out into Lane_Human rather than left here. Every path that changes `STAGING/` writes its render-log entry in the SAME commit as the change, because a log push that can fail on its own is exactly how a preview vanishes with nothing on the branch saying why."
msgstr ""

#: processes/feature-staging.bpmn:168
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Say what is going — size and file count — then remove STAGING/<slug>/ and append `removed` to the render log in the SAME commit, so a preview cannot vanish without a record of who dispatched it and why. The slug is a dispatch input, so the tool re-checks it by value rather than trusting the guard."
msgstr ""

